      "content": "From a scientific perspective, advocates often cite the efficacy and proven reduction in severe disease, hospitalization, and death that high vaccination rates achieve in population studies, supporting the \"duty to protect the community\" argument.\n\nCivil liberty arguments frequently lean on the legal doctrine of \"bodily integrity,\" asserting that government power to compel medical treatment must be extremely narrow and highly justified to meet constitutional standards, often referencing the right to reject medical intervention.\n\nThey also emphasize the scientific right to \"informed consent,\" arguing that a true public mandate bypasses the necessary process of a fully uncoerced, risk-aware individual decision.",
